  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tied through five innings until Jazz broke it open in the sixth.",
    "what_this_means": "Detroit scored first, but this team doesn't surrender to early deficits. They trailed 3-1 after three innings and clawed back, the lineup finding Rod\u00f3n's window of opportunity while the bullpen shut down the middle innings hard. Bednar closed it without drama. This is what stabilizing looks like: a starter who eats five and a third, three relievers who combine for two and a third scoreless, and one hitter. Jazz with his two-run swing. Who decides the game when it mattered. The offense couldn't find much (nine hits, thirteen strikeouts), but they didn't need much. They scored the right run at the right moment, converted one of eight RISP situations into the go-ahead. That's the opposite of waste.",
    "what_to_watch": "The division pressure stays constant. The window to win games like this one. Close, ugly, defensible. Closes fast. Jazz gave them the tiebreaker; the bullpen held the door. This only works if both jobs get done.",
